+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+  <meta charset="UTF-8">
+  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
+  <meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
+  <title>Privacy | The Daily Grind</title>
+  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/styles.css">
+</head>
+<body>
+  <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
+    <a href="/" class="logo">THE DAILY GRIND</a>
+    <a href="/">Back to the coffee</a>
+  </nav>
+  <main class="container policy">
+    <p class="eyebrow">Our privacy commitments</p>
+    <h1>Good coffee.<br>A little less data.</h1>
+    <p>We keep this website simple so you can explore without creating an account or handing over personal details.</p>
+    <p>Updated October 16, 2026 · Applies to this informational website.</p>
+    <aside class="privacy-note" aria-label="Privacy at a glance">
+      <strong>Your visit, at a glance</strong>
+      <ul>
+        <li>No analytics or advertising trackers</li>
+        <li>No cookies or browser storage</li>
+        <li>No personal information forms</li>
+        <li>Images and styles served directly by this site</li>
+      </ul>
+    </aside>
+    <section>
+      <h2>We collect less from the start</h2>
+      <p>This site does not request your name, email, location, or payment details. Account, rewards, and ordering services are not currently implemented. We do not build visitor profiles, sell personal data, or use fingerprinting.</p>
+    </section>
+    <section>
+      <h2>What happens when you visit</h2>
+      <p>Your browser sends ordinary connection information, including your IP address and requested page, to deliver the site. The application does not write access logs, retain request details, or store visitor data in a database.</p>
+      <p>The hosting provider or network infrastructure may process connection information independently. Its logging and retention settings must be reviewed for each deployment; application settings alone cannot control those records.</p>
+    </section>
+    <section>
+      <h2>Fewer third parties</h2>
+      <p>Your browser loads no third-party scripts, fonts, or images. Our coffee photograph is sourced from Unsplash and hosted locally, so viewing it does not connect your browser to Unsplash.</p>
+      <p>Our review process requires checking a provider’s purpose, data access, retention, security practices, and subprocessors before adding a service. No independent third-party privacy audit has been completed for this site.</p>
+    </section>
+    <section>
+      <h2>Secure handling by default</h2>
+      <p>The site restricts external connections, scripts, forms, framing, and access to device features. It sends no referrer information and asks browsers not to cache responses. Production hosting must use HTTPS to protect data in transit.</p>
+    </section>
+    <section>
+      <h2>Your choices</h2>
+      <p>You can browse without accepting optional tracking because none is installed. This application keeps no visitor profile or saved preferences to access, export, or delete. For questions about hosting records, contact the site operator through your existing contact channel; this site has no online request form.</p>
+    </section>
+    <section>
+      <h2>If the site changes</h2>
+      <p>Any new account, order, payment, or analytics feature needs its own data review and an updated notice before it launches. Optional data collection must be off by default and have a clear purpose, retention limit, and deletion process.</p>
+    </section>
+    <a href="/" class="btn">Back to The Daily Grind</a>
+  </main>
+  <footer><p>&copy; 2026 The Daily Grind Coffee Co.</p></footer>
+</body>
+</html>
